{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117886","id":3454555013,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7N6FOF","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117886","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117886.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117886.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117886","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117886/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117886/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117886/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/4c1b3f4f354bc2082c19141f18e53ef5eeaa05c4","number":117886,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[DRAFT] Audio: Implement `play_delayed` and `play_relative`","user":{"login":"PizzaLovers007","id":10912951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTEyOTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10912951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007","html_url":"https://github.com/PizzaLovers007","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is a proof of concept rewrite of #107226 that moves the silence frames logic back into AudioServer and changes the strategy to a delay-based/relative implementation. It also introduces the `play_relative` method that allows sounds to be played relative to another playback.\r\n\r\n`play_relative` calculates the necessary delay in the audio thread by adding a oneshot mix callback to the AudioServer. Unfortunately, due to `SafeList`'s implementation, the mix callbacks are processed in reverse-order of how they are added, which can cause issues when playbacks are \"chained\" together (playback A relative to playback B relative to playback C). \r\n\r\nSimilar to #117781, this still has the game/main thread performance issues due to AudioStreamPlayerInternal's process taking O(N^2) time with N active playbacks in the AudioServer. Additionally, pausing the base playback after calling `play_relative` does not change the calculated delay (new playback plays as if the base was not paused).\r\n\r\nDemo project: [MetronomeDelay.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26291778/MetronomeDelay.zip)\r\n\r\nTODOs:\r\n\r\n* ScheduledAudioStreamPlayer2D/3D counterparts\r\n* Fix game frame performance with many scheduled sounds\r\n* Address issues with `play_relative` (paused playbacks and mix callback ordering)\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for new contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":572781997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1NzI3ODE5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:a